WEBVTT

00:01:04.967 --> 00:01:06.800
What the?!

00:02:54.633 --> 00:02:56.900
Okay, i think i found a way

00:02:56.934 --> 00:02:58.900
We can bypass that
construction just east of here.

00:02:58.934 --> 00:03:02.067
We might even make pennsylvania
faster than we thought.

00:03:02.101 --> 00:03:03.501
Yeah.

00:03:03.534 --> 00:03:05.800
Problem is we're not
going to pennsylvania.

00:03:05.834 --> 00:03:07.834
Wait... what?

00:03:07.867 --> 00:03:10.267
I just got a call from an old friend.

00:03:10.301 --> 00:03:12.267
Her father was killed last night.

00:03:12.301 --> 00:03:13.800
She thinks it might
be our kind of thing.

00:03:13.834 --> 00:03:15.000
What?

00:03:15.034 --> 00:03:16.434
Yeah, believe me,

00:03:16.468 --> 00:03:19.934
<i>She never would've called,
never, if she didn't need us.</i>

00:03:21.967 --> 00:03:23.900
Come on. You coming or what?

00:03:35.134 --> 00:03:37.633
By "old friend," you mean...

00:03:37.667 --> 00:03:39.900
A friend that's not new.

00:03:39.934 --> 00:03:41.134
Yeah, thanks.

00:03:41.167 --> 00:03:44.468
So, her name's cassie, huh?

00:03:44.501 --> 00:03:46.201
You never mentioned her.

00:03:46.234 --> 00:03:48.267
Didn't i? No.

00:03:48.301 --> 00:03:50.934
Yeah, we went out. You
mean you dated someone?

00:03:50.967 --> 00:03:54.234
For more than one night?

00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:56.900
Am i speaking a language
you're not getting here?

00:03:56.934 --> 00:03:59.401
Dad and i were working
a job in athens, ohio.

00:03:59.434 --> 00:04:02.301
She was finishing up college.
We went out for a couple weeks.

00:04:02.334 --> 00:04:03.934
And?

00:04:07.234 --> 00:04:09.000
Look, it's terrible about her dad,

00:04:09.034 --> 00:04:11.667
But it kind of sounds like
a standard car accident.

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:13.967
I'm not seeing how it
fits with what we do.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:17.201
Which, by the way, how
does she know what we do?

00:04:21.733 --> 00:04:24.667
You told her. You told her the secret.

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:26.667
Our big family rule number one...

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:28.967
We do what we do and
we shut up about it.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:31.600
For a year and a half, i do
nothing but lie to jessica,

00:04:31.633 --> 00:04:34.301
And you go out with this
chick in ohio a couple of times

00:04:34.334 --> 00:04:36.568
And you tell her everything?

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:37.600
Dean!

00:04:37.633 --> 00:04:39.600
Yeah, looks like.

00:04:44.167 --> 00:04:46.234
Anderson: It's a
newspaper we put out here,

00:04:46.235 --> 00:04:48.067
Not a bulletin for the mayor's office.

00:04:48.101 --> 00:04:49.867
Get off your soapbox, jimmy.

00:04:49.900 --> 00:04:52.134
I'm urging a little discretion is all.

00:04:52.167 --> 00:04:55.234
No, i think you're telling
us what you want us to print

00:04:55.267 --> 00:04:57.167
And what you want us to sit on.

00:04:57.201 --> 00:04:58.967
I know you're upset, cassie.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:00.600
I liked your dad a lot.

00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:04.000
But i think your grief
is clouding your judgment.

00:05:04.034 --> 00:05:06.867
Two black people were killed
on the same stretch of road

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:08.667
In the same way in three weeks.

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:10.468
Jimmy, you're too close to this.

00:05:10.501 --> 00:05:12.900
Those guys were friends of yours.

00:05:12.934 --> 00:05:18.301
Again, i'm very sorry for your loss.

00:05:27.733 --> 00:05:30.234
Dean.

00:05:30.267 --> 00:05:31.834
Hey, cassie.

00:05:37.934 --> 00:05:40.201
This is my brother, sam.

00:05:43.967 --> 00:05:45.568
I'm sorry about your dad.

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:49.468
Yeah, me, too.

00:05:53.267 --> 00:05:56.101
My mother's in pretty bad shape.

00:05:56.134 --> 00:05:57.767
I've been staying with her.

00:05:57.800 --> 00:06:00.267
I wish she wouldn't go off by herself.

00:06:00.301 --> 00:06:02.667
She's been snervous and frightened.

00:06:02.700 --> 00:06:04.301
She was worried about dad.

00:06:04.334 --> 00:06:05.667
Why?

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:06.700
He was scared.

00:06:06.733 --> 00:06:08.267
He was seeing things.

00:06:08.301 --> 00:06:09.568
Like what?

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:12.468
He swore he saw an awful-Looking
black truck following him.

00:06:12.501 --> 00:06:14.867
A truck? Who was the driver?

00:06:14.900 --> 00:06:17.900
He didn't talk about a
driver, just the truck.

00:06:17.934 --> 00:06:20.501
He said it would appear and disappear.

00:06:20.534 --> 00:06:23.367
And in the accident,
dad's truck was dented

00:06:23.401 --> 00:06:26.501
Like it had been slammed
into by something big.

00:06:26.534 --> 00:06:27.733
Thanks.

00:06:27.767 --> 00:06:31.301
Now, you're sure this
dent wasn't there before?

00:06:31.334 --> 00:06:33.367
He sold cars, always drove a new one.

00:06:33.401 --> 00:06:35.468
There wasn't a scratch on that thing.

00:06:35.501 --> 00:06:39.301
It had rained hard that night.
There was mud everywhere.

00:06:39.334 --> 00:06:44.034
There was a distinct set of
muddy tracks from dad's car

00:06:44.067 --> 00:06:47.101
Leading right...

00:06:47.134 --> 00:06:50.101
To the edge where he went over.

00:06:51.501 --> 00:06:54.334
One set of tracks... his.

00:06:54.367 --> 00:06:57.034
And the first person killed
was a friend of your father's?

00:06:57.067 --> 00:06:58.468
Best friend... clayton solmes.

00:06:58.501 --> 00:07:00.201
They owned a car dealership together.

00:07:00.234 --> 00:07:04.101
Same thing... dent, no tracks.

00:07:04.134 --> 00:07:07.600
And the cops said exactly
what they said about dad...

00:07:07.633 --> 00:07:09.301
"He lost control of his car."

00:07:09.334 --> 00:07:11.534
Can you think of why your father
and partner might be targets?

00:07:11.568 --> 00:07:13.000
No.

00:07:13.034 --> 00:07:15.034
You think this vanishing
truck ran him off the road?

00:07:15.067 --> 00:07:18.767
When you say it aloud like that...

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:24.134
Listen, i'm a little skeptical
about this ghost stuff

00:07:24.167 --> 00:07:26.667
Or whatever it is you guys are into.

00:07:26.700 --> 00:07:28.201
Skeptical.

00:07:28.234 --> 00:07:30.700
If i remember, i think
you said i was nuts.

00:07:30.733 --> 00:07:32.568
That was then.

00:07:32.600 --> 00:07:34.867
Hmm.

00:07:36.867 --> 00:07:39.468
I just know that i can't
explain what happened up there,

00:07:39.501 --> 00:07:41.167
So i called you.

00:07:42.733 --> 00:07:45.468
Mom. Where have you been?

00:07:45.501 --> 00:07:49.534
I had no idea you'd
invited friends over.

00:07:49.568 --> 00:07:53.900
Mom, this is dean, a friend
of mine from... college,

00:07:53.934 --> 00:07:56.468
And his brother, sam.

00:07:56.501 --> 00:08:00.800
Well, l-L-L-I
won't interrupt you.

00:08:00.834 --> 00:08:02.067
Mrs. Robinson? Hmm?

00:08:02.101 --> 00:08:04.534
We're sorry for your loss.

00:08:04.568 --> 00:08:07.534
We'd like to talk to you for
a minute, if you don't mind.

00:08:07.568 --> 00:08:11.900
I'm really not up to that just now.

00:09:07.301 --> 00:09:09.900
Dd: Jimmy meant something to this town.

00:09:09.934 --> 00:09:11.633
He was one of our best.

00:09:11.667 --> 00:09:14.167
It won't be the same without him.

00:09:14.201 --> 00:09:17.134
Our best seem to be dropping like flies.

00:09:17.167 --> 00:09:19.000
Clayton, my father, jimmy.

00:09:19.034 --> 00:09:21.800
What is it exactly you want me to do?

00:09:21.834 --> 00:09:25.800
Well, how about closing this
section of road for starters?

00:09:25.834 --> 00:09:28.000
Close the main road, the
only road in and out of town?

00:09:28.034 --> 00:09:32.134
Accidents happen, cassie. That's
what they are... accidents.

00:09:32.167 --> 00:09:34.568
Did the cops check for
denting on jimmy's car

00:09:34.600 --> 00:09:36.234
To see if it was pushed?

00:09:36.267 --> 00:09:37.434
Who's this?

00:09:37.468 --> 00:09:40.401
Dean and sam winchester, family friends.

00:09:40.434 --> 00:09:43.568
This is mayor harold todd.

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:46.767
There's one set of tracks...
one. Doesn't point to foul play.

00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:49.101
Mayor, the police and town officials

00:09:49.134 --> 00:09:50.867
Take their cues from you...
if you're indifferent about...

00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:52.167
Indifferent?

00:09:52.201 --> 00:09:55.034
Would you close the road
if the victims were white?

00:09:55.067 --> 00:09:57.867
You're suggesting i'm racist, cassie.

00:09:57.900 --> 00:10:01.434
I'm the last person you
should talk to like that.

00:10:01.468 --> 00:10:02.434
Why is that?

00:10:02.468 --> 00:10:04.667
Why don't you k your mother?

00:10:09.800 --> 00:10:13.534
I'll say this for her... she's fearless.

00:10:13.568 --> 00:10:14.600
Mm-Hmm.

00:10:14.633 --> 00:10:18.134
Bet she kicked your ass a coupleimes.

00:10:18.167 --> 00:10:21.800
What's interesting is you guys
never really look at each other

00:10:21.834 --> 00:10:22.934
At the same time.

00:10:22.967 --> 00:10:25.401
You look at her when she's not looking.

00:10:25.434 --> 00:10:27.834
She checks you out when you look away.

00:10:29.367 --> 00:10:33.201
It's just a... just an
interesting observation

00:10:33.234 --> 00:10:36.834
In a, you know,
observationally interesting way.

00:10:36.867 --> 00:10:39.568
You think we might have some
more pressing issues here?

00:10:39.600 --> 00:10:41.900
Hey, if i'm hitting a nerve...

00:10:41.934 --> 00:10:43.234
Oh, let's go.

00:10:58.201 --> 00:11:00.401
Excuse me. Are you ron stubbins?

00:11:00.434 --> 00:11:02.234
Friends with jimmy anderson?

00:11:02.267 --> 00:11:03.434
Who are you?

00:11:03.468 --> 00:11:06.067
We're with mr. Anderson's
insurance company.

00:11:06.101 --> 00:11:08.900
Just here to dot some
i's and cross some t's.

00:11:08.934 --> 00:11:11.201
We were just wondering,
had the deceased mentioned

00:11:11.234 --> 00:11:12.767
Any unusual recent experiences?

00:11:12.800 --> 00:11:14.234
What do you mean, "unusual"?

00:11:14.267 --> 00:11:16.067
Well, visions, hallucinations.

00:11:16.101 --> 00:11:19.000
It's all part of a medical
examination kind of thing.

00:11:19.034 --> 00:11:21.101
What company you say you were with?

00:11:21.134 --> 00:11:23.434
All tional mutual.

00:11:23.468 --> 00:11:27.034
Tell me, did he ever
mention seeing a truck,

00:11:27.067 --> 00:11:29.034
A big black truck?

00:11:29.067 --> 00:11:31.434
What the hell you talking
about? You even speaking english?

00:11:31.468 --> 00:11:34.867
Son, this truck, a big,
scary, monster-Looking thing?

00:11:34.900 --> 00:11:36.568
Yeah, actually, i think so.

00:11:36.600 --> 00:11:38.633
Hmm.

00:11:38.667 --> 00:11:40.301
What?

00:11:40.334 --> 00:11:41.934
I have heard of a truck like that.

00:11:41.967 --> 00:11:43.234
You have?

00:11:43.267 --> 00:11:44.267
Where?

00:11:44.301 --> 00:11:46.434
Not where... when.

00:11:46.468 --> 00:11:49.800
Back in the '60s, there
was a string of deaths.

00:11:49.834 --> 00:11:52.201
Black men.

00:11:52.234 --> 00:11:56.534
Stores they disappeared in
a big, nasty black truck.

00:11:56.568 --> 00:11:58.067
They ever catch the guy who did it?

00:11:58.101 --> 00:11:59.134
Never found him.

00:11:59.167 --> 00:12:03.800
Hell, not sure they even really looked.

00:12:03.834 --> 00:12:06.000
See, there was a time

00:12:06.034 --> 00:12:12.867
This town wasn't too
friendly to all its citizens.

00:12:15.234 --> 00:12:16.301
Thank you.

00:12:21.101 --> 00:12:22.101
Truck.

00:12:22.134 --> 00:12:23.568
Keeps coming up, doesn't it?

00:12:23.600 --> 00:12:25.834
<i>I was thinking. You heard
of the flying dutchman?</i>

00:12:25.867 --> 00:12:28.468
Yeah, a ghost ship infused
with the captain's evil spirit.

00:12:28.501 --> 00:12:30.034
It was basically a part of him.

00:12:30.067 --> 00:12:32.201
So, what if we're dealing
with the same thing?

00:12:32.234 --> 00:12:35.000
A phantom truck who's the
extension of some bastard ghost,

00:12:35.034 --> 00:12:36.201
Re-Enacting past crimes.

00:12:36.234 --> 00:12:38.067
The victims have all been black men.

00:12:38.101 --> 00:12:39.600
I think it's more than that.

00:12:39.633 --> 00:12:42.401
They all seem connected
to cassie and her family.

00:12:42.434 --> 00:12:44.600
All right, well, you work that angle.

00:12:44.633 --> 00:12:45.667
Go talk to her.

00:12:45.700 --> 00:12:46.934
Yeah, i will.

00:12:46.967 --> 00:12:49.201
Oh, and you might also want
to mention that other thing.

00:12:49.234 --> 00:12:51.767
What other thing?

00:12:51.800 --> 00:12:54.733
That serious unfinished business.

00:12:54.767 --> 00:12:58.367
Dean, what is going on between you two?

00:12:58.401 --> 00:13:00.834
So maybe we were a little
bit more involved than i said.

00:13:00.867 --> 00:13:03.834
Oh, okay, yeah.

00:13:03.867 --> 00:13:05.900
Okay, a lot more... maybe.

00:13:05.934 --> 00:13:09.034
I told her the secret about
what we do, and i shouldn't have.

00:13:09.067 --> 00:13:12.034
Look, man, everybody's got to
open up to someone sometime.

00:13:12.067 --> 00:13:13.334
Yeah, i don't.

00:13:13.367 --> 00:13:16.600
It was stupid to get that
close. I mean, look how it ended.

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:19.600
Would you stop?

00:13:21.501 --> 00:13:23.468
Blink or something.

00:13:23.501 --> 00:13:25.067
You loved her.

00:13:25.101 --> 00:13:26.234
Oh, god.

00:13:26.267 --> 00:13:30.800
You were in love with
her, but you dumped her.

00:13:33.201 --> 00:13:35.767
Oh, wow.

00:13:37.501 --> 00:13:38.867
She dumped you.

00:13:38.900 --> 00:13:41.700
Get in the car.

00:13:41.733 --> 00:13:43.834
Get in the car!

00:13:59.034 --> 00:14:00.367
Dean.

00:14:00.401 --> 00:14:01.934
Hey. Hey.

00:14:01.967 --> 00:14:04.101
Come on in.

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:09.834
So, you busy?

00:14:09.867 --> 00:14:11.367
The paper is doing a tribute to jimmy.

00:14:11.401 --> 00:14:16.401
I was just going through
his stuff, his awards,

00:14:16.434 --> 00:14:19.334
Trying to find the words.

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:23.167
That's got to be tough.

00:14:23.201 --> 00:14:25.600
For years this family owned
the paper, the dorians.

00:14:25.633 --> 00:14:27.600
They had a whites-Only staff policy.

00:14:27.633 --> 00:14:31.534
After they sold it, jimmy
became the first black reporter.

00:14:31.568 --> 00:14:34.401
He became editor.

00:14:34.434 --> 00:14:36.568
He taught me everything.

00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:38.034
Where's your brother?

00:14:39.834 --> 00:14:41.134
Not here.

00:14:41.167 --> 00:14:43.334
All right, so, what brings you here?

00:14:43.367 --> 00:14:45.401
I'm trying to find the connection

00:14:45.434 --> 00:14:46.934
Between the three victims.

00:14:46.967 --> 00:14:48.434
By the way, did you talk to your mom

00:14:48.468 --> 00:14:50.501
About what todd said
about not being a racist?

00:14:50.534 --> 00:14:51.700
I did.

00:14:51.733 --> 00:14:55.000
She didn't want to talk about it.

00:14:57.534 --> 00:15:01.167
So, just then, why did you
ask where my brother was?

00:15:01.201 --> 00:15:02.600
Nothing. Not important.

00:15:02.633 --> 00:15:05.633
Could it be because without
him here it'just you and me

00:15:05.667 --> 00:15:07.501
And not you, me, and sam,
which would be easier?

00:15:07.534 --> 00:15:08.800
It's not easier.

00:15:08.834 --> 00:15:10.501
Look...

00:15:10.534 --> 00:15:13.234
No, forget it. It's fine.

00:15:13.267 --> 00:15:16.301
Keep it strictly business.

00:15:16.334 --> 00:15:18.800
I forgot you do that.

00:15:18.834 --> 00:15:21.367
Do what?

00:15:21.401 --> 00:15:23.767
Oh, whenever we get...

00:15:23.800 --> 00:15:26.034
What's the word, close?...

00:15:26.067 --> 00:15:28.834
Anywhere in the neighborhood
of emotional vulnerability,

00:15:28.867 --> 00:15:31.267
You back off or make some joke

00:15:31.301 --> 00:15:33.301
Or find any way to shut the door on me.

00:15:33.334 --> 00:15:35.234
Oh, that's hilarious.

00:15:35.267 --> 00:15:38.034
See, i'm not the one who
took that big, final door

00:15:38.067 --> 00:15:39.867
And slammed it behind
me, and i'm not the one

00:15:39.900 --> 00:15:41.367
Who took the key and buried it.

00:15:41.401 --> 00:15:43.101
Are we done with this metaphor?

00:15:43.134 --> 00:15:44.733
All i'm saying is i was totally
up front with you back then

00:15:44.767 --> 00:15:45.800
And you nailed me with it.

00:15:45.834 --> 00:15:47.767
The guy i'm hoping might be in my future

00:15:47.800 --> 00:15:49.700
Tells me he professionally pops ghosts.

00:15:49.733 --> 00:15:51.134
Those weren't the words i used.

00:15:51.167 --> 00:15:53.334
And he has to leave too
work with his father. I did.

00:15:53.367 --> 00:15:55.000
All i could think was,
if you want out, fine.

00:15:55.034 --> 00:15:56.967
But don't tell me this insane story.

00:15:57.000 --> 00:15:58.401
It was the truth, cassie,

00:15:58.434 --> 00:16:00.900
It didn't sound so insane the
minute you thought i could help.

00:16:00.934 --> 00:16:03.000
Back then i thought you
just wanted to dump me.

00:16:03.034 --> 00:16:05.800
Whoa, let's not forget
who dumped who, okay?

00:16:05.834 --> 00:16:08.000
I thought it was what you wanted.

00:16:08.034 --> 00:16:09.134
Well, it wasn't.

00:16:09.167 --> 00:16:10.967
I didn't mean to hurt you.

00:16:11.000 --> 00:16:11.967
Well, you did.

00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:13.934
I'm sorry. Yeah, me, too.

00:18:16.367 --> 00:18:19.000
Absolutely.

00:18:19.033 --> 00:18:22.033
Actually, we were always
pretty good at fighting.

00:18:22.067 --> 00:18:24.534
This, we were good at.

00:18:24.567 --> 00:18:28.900
It's all the other stuff, not so much.

00:18:28.933 --> 00:18:31.667
Hey, i tried.

00:18:31.701 --> 00:18:35.734
I told you who i really was.
It was a big first for me.

00:18:35.768 --> 00:18:37.933
Why'd you tell me?

00:18:37.967 --> 00:18:40.367
I don't know.

00:18:43.367 --> 00:18:46.701
I guess i couldn't lie to you.

00:18:49.501 --> 00:18:51.567
Dean...

00:18:51.601 --> 00:18:55.134
When you told me that story,

00:18:55.167 --> 00:18:56.933
It scared the hell out of me.

00:18:56.967 --> 00:19:01.300
I thought you were nuts, dangerous even.

00:19:01.334 --> 00:19:04.933
Actually...

00:19:04.967 --> 00:19:09.267
Maybe i was looking for
a reason to walk away.

00:19:09.300 --> 00:19:15.000
In my work i see some horrible things,

00:19:15.033 --> 00:19:17.768
Things that can't be explained.

00:19:17.801 --> 00:19:19.200
I deal with them.

00:19:19.234 --> 00:19:21.834
But working things out with you?

00:19:21.868 --> 00:19:24.501
I'm a scary one, all right.

00:19:24.534 --> 00:19:26.067
Hmm.

00:19:31.834 --> 00:19:36.434
Well, usually thgs get worked out

00:19:36.467 --> 00:19:39.234
When you really want them to.

00:19:43.534 --> 00:19:47.900
Yeah, but i'm still really
involved in my dad's work.

00:19:50.067 --> 00:19:55.601
No more excuses, okay? From you or me.

00:19:55.634 --> 00:19:56.834
Okay.

00:20:14.100 --> 00:20:16.900
Yeah

00:20:16.933 --> 00:20:20.033
You're kidding.

00:20:24.200 --> 00:20:25.768
And he's with me.

00:20:27.768 --> 00:20:30.033
Where were you last night?

00:20:30.067 --> 00:20:33.067
You didn't make it back to the motel.

00:20:33.100 --> 00:20:34.200
Nope.

00:20:34.234 --> 00:20:36.167
I'm guessing you guys worked things out.

00:20:36.200 --> 00:20:38.200
We'll be working things
out when we're 90.

00:20:38.234 --> 00:20:39.501
So, what happened?

00:20:39.534 --> 00:20:41.834
Every bone crushed, internal
organs turned to pudding.

00:20:41.868 --> 00:20:43.067
The cops are all stumped,

00:20:43.100 --> 00:20:44.967
But it's almost like
something ran him over.

00:20:45.000 --> 00:20:46.534
Something like a truck? Yep.

00:20:46.567 --> 00:20:48.634
Tracks? Nope.

00:20:48.667 --> 00:20:50.734
What was the mayor doing here anyway?

00:20:50.768 --> 00:20:53.200
He owned the property.
Bought it a few weeks ago.

00:20:53.234 --> 00:20:55.367
Yeah, but he's white.
Doesn't fit the pattern.

00:20:55.401 --> 00:20:57.234
Killings didn't happen up on the road.

00:20:57.267 --> 00:21:00.134
That doesn't fit, either.

00:21:06.067 --> 00:21:07.334
Thanks.

00:21:07.367 --> 00:21:09.701
I'm trying to find some
link between those killings

00:21:09.734 --> 00:21:11.501
In the '60s and what's going on now.

00:21:11.534 --> 00:21:13.467
There wasn't a lot
about it in the paper.

00:21:13.501 --> 00:21:16.334
Not surprising. Probably
minimal-Police-Work deal.

00:21:16.367 --> 00:21:18.667
Back then, equal justice under the law

00:21:18.701 --> 00:21:20.601
Wasn't too literal around here.

00:21:23.200 --> 00:21:24.367
Yeah?

00:21:24.401 --> 00:21:25.933
Sam: Okay, the courthouse records

00:21:25.967 --> 00:21:29.100
Show that mr. And mrs. Mayor
bought an abandoned property.

00:21:29.134 --> 00:21:31.100
The previous owner
was the dorian family,

00:21:31.134 --> 00:21:32.534
For like 150 years.

00:21:32.567 --> 00:21:33.868
Dorian? Yeah.

00:21:33.900 --> 00:21:36.300
Didn't you say the dorian
family used to own this paper?

00:21:36.334 --> 00:21:38.300
Along with most everything
else around here.

00:21:38.334 --> 00:21:40.467
Real pillars of the town.

00:21:40.501 --> 00:21:41.768
Right, right.

00:21:44.300 --> 00:21:45.734
That's interesting.

00:21:45.768 --> 00:21:47.701
What?

00:21:47.734 --> 00:21:50.801
This cyrus dorian, he
vanished in april of '63.

00:21:50.834 --> 00:21:53.801
The case was investigated
but never solved.

00:21:53.834 --> 00:21:56.167
It was the time the string
of murders was going on.

00:21:56.200 --> 00:21:57.868
Well, i pulled a bunch of
paper up on the dorian place.

00:21:57.900 --> 00:21:59.567
It must've been in bad shape
when the mayor bought it.

00:21:59.601 --> 00:22:01.100
Why is that?

00:22:01.134 --> 00:22:02.801
The first thing he did
was bulldoze the place.

00:22:02.834 --> 00:22:05.501
Mayor todd knocked down the dorianlace?

00:22:05.534 --> 00:22:09.200
It was a big deal. One of
the oldest local houses left.

00:22:09.234 --> 00:22:10.801
It made the front page.

00:22:10.834 --> 00:22:11.967
You got a date?

00:22:12.000 --> 00:22:15.267
Uh... the 3rd of last month.

00:22:19.467 --> 00:22:22.933
Mayor todd bulldozed the
dorian family home on the 3rd.

00:22:22.967 --> 00:22:25.834
The first killing was the very next day.

00:23:48.300 --> 00:23:49.768
Dean!

00:23:53.980 --> 00:23:56.047
Maybe you could throw
a couple shots in that.

00:23:56.980 --> 00:24:00.714
You didn't see who
was driving the truck?

00:24:02.114 --> 00:24:03.514
It seemed to be no one.

00:24:06.413 --> 00:24:08.614
Everything was moving so fast.

00:24:10.317 --> 00:24:15.617
And then it was just gone.
Why didn't it kill us?

00:24:15.651 --> 00:24:19.317
Whatever is controlling the
truck wants you afraid first.

00:24:19.350 --> 00:24:24.517
Mrs. Robinson, cassie said
that your husband saw the truck

00:24:24.551 --> 00:24:27.183
Before he died.

00:24:27.217 --> 00:24:28.517
Mom?

00:24:28.551 --> 00:24:30.018
Hmm?

00:24:30.984 --> 00:24:33.851
Martin was under a lot of stress.

00:24:33.884 --> 00:24:35.851
You can't be sure about
what he was seeing.

00:24:35.884 --> 00:24:38.250
Well, after tonight i think
we can be reasonably sure

00:24:38.284 --> 00:24:39.651
That he was seeing a truck.

00:24:39.684 --> 00:24:44.984
What happened tonight, you
and cassie are marked, okay?

00:24:45.018 --> 00:24:47.350
Your daughter could die,
so if you know something,

00:24:47.384 --> 00:24:49.317
Now would be a really good
time to tell us about it.

00:24:49.350 --> 00:24:51.217
Dean... yes.

00:24:51.250 --> 00:24:53.918
Yes, he said he saw a truck.

00:24:53.951 --> 00:24:56.150
Did he know who it belonged to?

00:24:56.183 --> 00:24:58.484
He thought he did. Who was that?

00:25:00.551 --> 00:25:03.517
Cyrus...

00:25:03.551 --> 00:25:06.617
A man named cyrus.

00:25:09.951 --> 00:25:12.350
Is this cyrus?

00:25:12.384 --> 00:25:17.984
Cyrus dorian died
more than 40 years ago.

00:25:18.018 --> 00:25:22.284
How do you know he died, mrs. Robinson?

00:25:23.984 --> 00:25:26.183
The paper said he went missing.

00:25:26.217 --> 00:25:28.551
How do you know he died?

00:25:28.584 --> 00:25:32.217
We were all very young.

00:25:34.217 --> 00:25:37.083
I dated cyrus a while.

00:25:37.117 --> 00:25:40.183
I was also seeing martin,
in secret of course

00:25:40.217 --> 00:25:46.450
'Cause interracial couples
didn't go over too well then.

00:25:46.484 --> 00:25:48.984
When i broke it off with cyrus,

00:25:49.018 --> 00:25:51.918
And when he found out about martin...

00:25:51.951 --> 00:25:57.417
I don't know... he changed.

00:25:57.450 --> 00:26:03.250
His hatred... his
hatred was frightening.

00:26:03.284 --> 00:26:04.751
The string of murders.

00:26:04.784 --> 00:26:07.250
There were rumors,

00:26:07.284 --> 00:26:10.117
People of color disappearing
into some kind oa truck.

00:26:13.484 --> 00:26:16.217
Nothing was ever done.

00:26:21.517 --> 00:26:23.417
Martin and...

00:26:25.417 --> 00:26:29.717
Martin and i, we were gonna be married

00:26:29.751 --> 00:26:31.751
In that little church near here,

00:26:31.784 --> 00:26:34.684
But last minute, we decided to elope

00:26:34.717 --> 00:26:37.018
'Cause we didn't want all the attention.

00:26:37.050 --> 00:26:38.284
And cyrus?

00:26:45.018 --> 00:26:50.317
The day we set for the wedding

00:26:50.350 --> 00:26:55.884
Was the day someone
set fire to the church.

00:27:03.984 --> 00:27:09.183
There was a children's
choir practicing in there.

00:27:11.651 --> 00:27:14.784
They all died.

00:27:17.217 --> 00:27:19.784
Did the attacks stop after that?

00:27:19.817 --> 00:27:22.751
No, there was one more.

00:27:24.751 --> 00:27:29.551
One night that truck came for martin.

00:27:32.018 --> 00:27:34.484
Cyrus beat him something terrible,

00:27:39.183 --> 00:27:42.384
But martin... you see, martin got loose

00:27:42.417 --> 00:27:45.250
And he started hitting cyrus

00:27:45.284 --> 00:27:49.484
And he just kept hitting
him and hitting him.

00:28:00.751 --> 00:28:03.083
Why didn't you call the cops?

00:28:07.417 --> 00:28:10.617
This was 40 years ago.

00:28:10.651 --> 00:28:14.250
He called on his friends...

00:28:14.284 --> 00:28:16.217
Clayton, solmes, and jimmy anderson...

00:28:16.250 --> 00:28:19.584
And they put cyrus' body into the truck

00:28:19.617 --> 00:28:24.183
And then rolled it into the
swamp at the edge of his land

00:28:24.217 --> 00:28:30.717
And all three of them kept
that secret all these years.

00:28:32.751 --> 00:28:34.183
And now all three are gone.

00:28:34.217 --> 00:28:35.317
So is mayor todd.

00:28:37.083 --> 00:28:40.384
Now, he said that you of all people

00:28:40.417 --> 00:28:42.217
Would know that he is not a racist.

00:28:42.250 --> 00:28:43.284
Why would he say that?

00:28:43.317 --> 00:28:44.317
He was a good man.

00:28:44.350 --> 00:28:47.617
He was a young deputy back then,

00:28:47.651 --> 00:28:49.384
Investigating cyrus's disappearance.

00:28:49.417 --> 00:28:55.117
Once he figured out what
martin and the others had done,

00:28:55.150 --> 00:29:00.951
He he did nothing

00:29:02.617 --> 00:29:05.684
Because he also knew
what cyrus had done.

00:29:08.817 --> 00:29:10.484
Why didn't you tell me?

00:29:10.517 --> 00:29:13.183
I thought i was protecting them.

00:29:15.250 --> 00:29:20.350
And now there's no one left to protect.

00:29:20.384 --> 00:29:21.751
Yes, there is.

00:29:31.018 --> 00:29:33.117
Oh, my life was so simple.

00:29:33.150 --> 00:29:37.617
Just school, exams,

00:29:37.651 --> 00:29:41.150
Papers on polycentric cultural norms.

00:29:41.183 --> 00:29:45.083
So i guess i saved you
from a boring existence.

00:29:45.117 --> 00:29:47.284
Occasionally i miss boring.

00:29:49.050 --> 00:29:50.617
So, this killer truck...

00:29:50.651 --> 00:29:54.517
I miss conversations that didn't
start with "this killer truck."

00:29:54.551 --> 00:29:56.984
Ah...

00:29:57.018 --> 00:29:58.951
All right, well, this cyrus guy,

00:29:58.984 --> 00:30:01.617
Evil on a level that
infected even his truck.

00:30:01.651 --> 00:30:05.150
When he died, the swamp became his tomb

00:30:05.183 --> 00:30:07.517
And his spirit was dormant for 40 years.

00:30:07.551 --> 00:30:08.751
So, what woke it up?

00:30:08.784 --> 00:30:11.350
The construction on his
house or the destructi.

00:30:11.384 --> 00:30:12.484
Right.

00:30:12.517 --> 00:30:15.284
Demolition or remodeling
can awaken spirits,

00:30:15.317 --> 00:30:17.018
Make them restless.

00:30:17.050 --> 00:30:19.417
Like that theater in illinois.

00:30:19.450 --> 00:30:20.684
Yeah.

00:30:20.717 --> 00:30:22.717
And the guy who tears
down the family homestead,

00:30:22.751 --> 00:30:25.250
Harold todd, is the same guy

00:30:25.284 --> 00:30:28.817
That kept cyrus's murder
quiet and unsolved.

00:30:28.851 --> 00:30:31.018
So now his spirit is
awakened and out for blood.

00:30:31.050 --> 00:30:33.317
I guess. Who knows what
ghosts are thinking anyway.

00:30:33.350 --> 00:30:36.717
You know we're gonna have to
dredge that body from the swamp?

00:30:36.751 --> 00:30:38.350
Maman.

00:30:38.384 --> 00:30:40.717
You said it. Yeah.

00:30:40.751 --> 00:30:41.717
Hey.

00:30:41.751 --> 00:30:42.717
Hey.

00:30:42.751 --> 00:30:44.784
She's asleep.

00:30:44.817 --> 00:30:46.884
Now what?

00:30:46.918 --> 00:30:48.617
You stay put and look after her.

00:30:48.651 --> 00:30:50.717
And we'll be back.
Don't leave the house.

00:30:50.751 --> 00:30:52.951
Don't go getting all
authoritative on me.

00:30:52.984 --> 00:30:54.050
I hate it.

00:30:55.484 --> 00:30:58.217
Don't leave the house, please?

00:31:10.183 --> 00:31:12.918
You coming or what?

00:31:17.517 --> 00:31:21.117
Sam: All right, let's get her up.

00:31:22.684 --> 00:31:25.918
All right. Little more.

00:31:25.951 --> 00:31:27.183
Little more.

00:31:28.450 --> 00:31:30.651
Litt more.

00:31:30.684 --> 00:31:31.918
All right, stop.

00:31:40.551 --> 00:31:41.684
Nice.

00:31:41.717 --> 00:31:43.784
Hell yeah.

00:31:43.817 --> 00:31:45.183
Now i know what she sees in you.

00:31:45.217 --> 00:31:46.450
What?

00:31:46.484 --> 00:31:49.018
Come on, you can admit it.
You're still in love with her.

00:31:49.050 --> 00:31:50.317
Can we focus, please?

00:31:50.350 --> 00:31:52.183
I'm just saying, dean.

00:31:52.217 --> 00:31:53.217
Hold that.

00:31:53.250 --> 00:31:55.851
All right. What am i getting?

00:31:55.884 --> 00:31:57.450
Gas, flashlight. Got it, got it.

00:31:57.484 --> 00:31:58.984
All right, let's get this done.

00:31:59.018 --> 00:32:01.250
All right. Got it.

00:32:18.551 --> 00:32:20.083
All right, let's get to it.

00:32:35.651 --> 00:32:38.250
Think that'll do it?

00:32:44.083 --> 00:32:46.050
I guess not.

00:32:49.677 --> 00:32:51.577
So burning the body had
no effect on that thing?

00:32:51.610 --> 00:32:52.944
Sure it did. Now it's really pissed.

00:32:52.977 --> 00:32:54.910
But cyrus's ghost is gone, right, dean?

00:32:54.944 --> 00:32:56.710
Apparently not the part
that's fused with the truck.

00:32:56.984 --> 00:32:58.783
Where you going?

00:32:58.817 --> 00:33:01.184
Going for a little ride.
Gonna lead that thing away.

00:33:01.217 --> 00:33:03.017
That rusted piece of
crap, you got to burn it.

00:33:03.050 --> 00:33:04.651
How the hell am i supposed
to burn a truck, dean?

00:33:04.684 --> 00:33:06.517
I don't know. Figure something out.

00:33:06.891 --> 00:33:08.524
Figure something...

00:33:48.421 --> 00:33:50.588
Hey, you got to give me a minute.

00:33:50.620 --> 00:33:52.121
I don't have a minute!
What are we doing?!

00:33:52.154 --> 00:33:55.121
Uh... let me get back to you.

00:33:57.588 --> 00:33:59.121
Hey, cassie? Hey, it's sam.

00:33:59.154 --> 00:34:02.187
Okay, i need some information
and it has to be exactly right.

00:34:05.454 --> 00:34:07.154
All right, dean. This better be good!

00:34:07.187 --> 00:34:10.787
Where are you? I'm in the middle of
nowhere with a killer truck on my ass!

00:34:10.820 --> 00:34:13.020
It's like it knows i
put the torch to cyrus!

00:34:13.054 --> 00:34:14.720
Dean, listen to me. It's important.

00:34:14.753 --> 00:34:15.820
I have to know exactly where you are.

00:34:15.854 --> 00:34:18.254
Decatur road, about two
miles off the highway.

00:34:18.287 --> 00:34:20.054
Okay, headed east? Yes!

00:34:24.987 --> 00:34:28.187
Oh, you son of a bitch.

00:34:28.221 --> 00:34:29.454
Okay, uh, turn right.

00:34:36.454 --> 00:34:37.653
You make the turn?

00:34:37.687 --> 00:34:39.087
Yeah, i made the turn!

00:34:39.121 --> 00:34:40.854
Move this thing along a little faster!

00:34:40.887 --> 00:34:42.454
All right, you see a road up ahead?

00:34:42.488 --> 00:34:43.687
No!

00:34:43.720 --> 00:34:45.454
Wait, yes, i see it!

00:34:45.488 --> 00:34:47.087
Okay, turn left. What?!

00:34:54.588 --> 00:34:56.154
All right, now what?

00:34:56.187 --> 00:34:58.154
Go exactly 7/10ths of a mile and stop.

00:34:58.187 --> 00:35:00.854
Stop? Exactly 7/10ths, dean.

00:35:00.887 --> 00:35:03.254
7/10ths, 7/10ths.

00:35:32.720 --> 00:35:35.554
Dean, are you still there?

00:35:35.588 --> 00:35:37.254
Yeah. What's happening?

00:35:37.287 --> 00:35:39.254
It's just staring at me. What do i do?

00:35:39.287 --> 00:35:41.653
Just what you are doing...
bringing it to you.

00:35:41.687 --> 00:35:42.753
Wh...

00:35:59.820 --> 00:36:01.354
Come on, come on.

00:36:21.387 --> 00:36:24.054
Dean?

00:36:24.087 --> 00:36:25.287
You still there?

00:36:25.321 --> 00:36:28.154
Dean?

00:36:28.187 --> 00:36:30.588
Where'd it go?

00:36:30.620 --> 00:36:33.820
Dean, you're where the church was.

00:36:33.854 --> 00:36:35.087
What church?

00:36:35.121 --> 00:36:37.588
The place cyrus burned down
and murdered all those kids.

00:36:37.620 --> 00:36:39.221
There's not a whole lot left.

00:36:39.254 --> 00:36:40.954
Church ground is hallowed ground

00:36:40.987 --> 00:36:42.488
Whether the church
is still there or not.

00:36:42.521 --> 00:36:44.554
Evil spirits cross over hallowed ground,

00:36:44.588 --> 00:36:46.321
Sometimes they're destroyed.

00:36:46.354 --> 00:36:51.254
So i figured maybe that
would get rid of it.

00:36:51.287 --> 00:36:52.287
Maybe?

00:36:52.321 --> 00:36:53.620
Maybe?!

00:36:53.653 --> 00:36:56.354
What if you were wrong?!

00:36:58.121 --> 00:37:00.820
Honestly, that thought
hadn't occurred to me.

00:37:05.020 --> 00:37:07.321
"Well, that honestly
didn't occur to me."

00:37:13.321 --> 00:37:14.987
I'm gonna kill him.

00:37:21.974 --> 00:37:25.007
My mother says to tell you thanks again.

00:37:29.940 --> 00:37:32.841
This was a better goodbye
than the last time.

00:37:32.874 --> 00:37:34.808
Yeah, well, maybe this time

00:37:34.841 --> 00:37:37.107
It'll be a little less permanent.

00:37:37.140 --> 00:37:40.707
You know what?

00:37:40.741 --> 00:37:43.741
I'm a realist.

00:37:43.774 --> 00:37:46.707
I don't see much hope for us, dean.

00:37:50.374 --> 00:37:53.240
Well, i've seen stranger things happen.

00:37:53.274 --> 00:37:54.940
Hell of a lot stranger.

00:37:59.607 --> 00:38:01.474
Goodbye, dean.

00:38:01.507 --> 00:38:04.474
I'll see you, cassie.

00:38:04.507 --> 00:38:07.441
I will.

00:39:00.007 --> 00:39:02.107
I like her.

00:39:02.140 --> 00:39:03.474
Yeah.

00:39:05.808 --> 00:39:07.574
You meet someone like her,

00:39:07.607 --> 00:39:10.407
Ever make you wonder if it's worth it...

00:39:10.441 --> 00:39:14.541
Putting everything else
on hold, doing what we do?

00:39:27.107 --> 00:39:30.207
Why don't you wake me up
when it's my turn to drive?



00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.000
